new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5f35754
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# smallpt browser lab
+
+Kevin Beason’s [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/), compiled from C++ to WebAssembly with Emscripten. Open `index.html` through an HTTP server; rendering runs entirely on the device in a dedicated Web Worker.
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+npm start
+```
+
+The compiled JavaScript and `.wasm` are included, so serving the page does not require a compiler. The page starts rendering automatically. Randomize colors, edit the two sphere colors individually, change sample quality, reset the materials, or download the current image as PNG. Changing settings terminates the previous worker and starts a new render.
+
+## Build and check
+
+Install Emscripten and make `emcc` available, then:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+npm test
+```
+
+The smoke test executes the actual WebAssembly in Node, checking visible pixels, alpha, material changes, reset, and progressive accumulation. No browser automation is required.
+
+`vendor/smallpt/smallpt.cpp` is the unchanged upstream source. `renderer/smallpt.cpp` keeps its scene, ray intersections, Monte Carlo integrator, mirror and glass materials, and 2×2 tent-filtered camera sampling. Its browser adapter replaces `main` and PPM output with exported setup, material, row-rendering, and RGBA-buffer functions. It accumulates linear radiance and applies gamma conversion to each displayed pass (four samples per pixel). OpenMP is replaced by a Web Worker. Rows are rendered in chunks; full frames are transferred after each pass. Walls and lighting remain fixed when sphere colors change.
+
+`renderer/preview.png` is an actual 128-sample output of the same compiled renderer, used as a placeholder while the first client-side pass runs. Regenerate it with `node scripts/preview.cjs`. It is replaced by live pixels as soon as they arrive.
+
+Original renderer copyright © 2006–2008 Kevin Beason; MIT license is preserved in `vendor/smallpt/LICENSE.txt`.
